WEBVTT

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.580
Haruka, I'm going!

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:15.540
O-okay!

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:22.040
Jeez.
This time, your heart will melt down!

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.330
She's makin' a racket ALREADY!
This time, your heart will melt down!

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:23.830
She's makin' a racket ALREADY!
Ami Futami's debut album.

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:26.330
Ami Futami
DEBUT ALBUM!!!!
"Don't Forget the Positive"

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:24.750
Ami Futami's debut album.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:26.330
Advance orders have sold out!

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.410
I've heard the S.O.S.

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:34.330
Have you finally heard it?

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:50.330
In a cutesy way

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:53.830
Impure or pure, which character?

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:56.700
Maybe they're the same

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.200
The love beat is opened up full throttle

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:04.250
I've noticed, this is a special mission... I've got it

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:10.620
I'll show you for real, because I'll make it come true

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:14.500
In a world that's pierced through the skies

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:21.450
I felt a strange emotion, I liked you in an instant!

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:26.500
I'm sure I'll win with a smile

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:29.870
Sure enough a smile is the right way

00:01:29.870 --> 00:01:35.410
I was small and crying but I'll rise to the challenge

00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:37.750
I wonder what this palpitation is

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:41.080
I need a little medical attention

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:49.120
This feeling of slight fever could be your fault,
S.O.S!

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:01.830
Keyboard

00:01:57.540 --> 00:01:59.080
Pickup is all right.

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:02.580
Gap and vibration rates are
within acceptable ranges.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.540
Lowering it down!

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:09.500
Treat that carefully!
It's the only one we have.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:10.750
Ma'am!

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:12.660
Where's the connector for this?

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:14.080
Isn't it to the bottom right?

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:14.500
Oh, this?

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.750
Ritsuko.
Oh, this?

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:18.870
What happened to Imber?

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:21.120
We're preparing the Harmonizer.

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:23.330
Harmonizer?

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:26.080
I guess it's like a core regulation device.

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:29.540
If we can match adjustments
to the core and the frame,

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:32.620
we'll be able to draw out more
of the Imber's capabilities.

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:34.660
But why suddenly do this?

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:37.830
The chief and the others said that,
based on that fight you had last time,

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:41.160
we should try and come up
with some countermeasures.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:42.950
Last time...

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:50.790
So, this is for fighting?

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:55.450
Yes. True enough, these measures
are to combat Turiavita.

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:58.450
Oh. I see...

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:01.410
I'm sorry.

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:07.250
I understand how you're feeling, Haruka.
But as long as Turiavita exists-

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:10.290
Just what is Turiavita?

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:14.540
Why do they do those things?
Why would they steal iDOLs?

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:18.750
This concerns things that have yet to come.

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:21.790
Let's talk about this in detail.

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:28.290
Turiavita was once part of us,
the research department of Mondenkind.

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:32.830
But they wanted to use the iDOLs for evil.

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:36.830
Then, 16 years ago...

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:40.540
There was the incident that came to be
called the Dawn of the Purple Moon.

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:45.910
They tried to steal the iDOLs,
making them theirs alone.

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:48.700
That's when the Nubilum...?

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.080
Yes.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:54.370
Fortunately, some of the members
at the time took notice,

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:57.200
and we were able to keep our loss
to the Nubilum alone.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:05.450
In other words, Turiavita currently holds
just one the five iDOLs in existence.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:11.080
We have two. The whereabouts
of the other two are unknown.

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:12.660
But this...

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:14.450
You don't get it?

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:18.790
Improving the Imber's and the Nebula's
abilities isn't just for fighting.

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:21.290
It's also to create a difference in power,

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:24.080
making it more difficult for
Turiavita to make a move.

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:27.040
So it's to PREVENT fighting?

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:32.830
Yes. We don't want the iDOLs
to have to fight, either.

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:34.660
Azusa...

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:37.290
Ma'am, can you talk?

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:37.950
What is it?

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:41.160
We've gotten it ambulatory, but...

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:43.540
Any more than this just isn't...

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:48.580
We've hauled out the manual and are doing
our best, but it's going nowhere.

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:51.040
I see. Understood.

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:54.330
Sure enough, it's impossible
with our current members, eh?

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:57.250
What do you mean?

00:04:57.250 --> 00:05:01.410
To use it, you have to able
to distinguish the delicate, um...

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:06.200
timbres that the iDOLs emit.
It's very difficult.

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:07.620
Timbres?

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.950
We need her, do we?

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:13.290
Yes. But...

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:21.580
Huh? What is it?

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:22.830
Sir.

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:25.200
It's worth trying, I'd say.

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:26.450
Um...

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:30.080
Haruka, there's something
we'd like you to do.

00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:31.080
Ma'am?

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.080
Ami Futami?

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:37.080
You mean, THE Ami Futami?

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:40.080
Yeah! I surprised, too,

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:42.870
but apparently she used to be
a mechanic at Mondenkind

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:46.040
and she was in charge of this
"Harmonizer" thing.

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:48.950
A celebrity used to do that?

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:51.950
Anyway, they said she's busy
and no one can get hold of her,

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:55.450
so I should go see her in person
and tell her to come back.

00:05:55.700 --> 00:06:00.660
Jeez! I wondered why you suddenly
said to come the TV station...

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:02.950
Don't be calling me about
something like THAT!

00:06:02.950 --> 00:06:06.290
Well, I was nervous by myself...

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:09.660
Oh, but listen! There may be
some celebrities there!

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:12.950
You're the only one who'd be
interested in something like that.

00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:14.040
Whoa! Look!

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:15.540
Wh-what? Who?

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:17.000
Gotcha.

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:21.330
Look, let's just go!

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:22.160
So you ARE interested.

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:23.120
Shut up!
So you ARE interested.

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:26.120
Stage No. 5.

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:28.200
This is the place, right?

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:32.700
Yeah. The receptionist
said she was here on standby...

00:06:46.950 --> 00:06:48.500
That's Ami?

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:51.910
Looks like it. But she's PLAINER
than you'd think, huh?

00:06:53.950 --> 00:06:54.450
Um-!

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:56.040
Jeez!

00:06:56.040 --> 00:07:00.160
Idiot! What are you doing?!
What if she were recording?

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:02.330
S-sorry!

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:04.870
It's all right. I'm on break right now.

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:10.910
Those uniforms... You're from Gyokuto High
School, aren't you? Nice to meet you.

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:12.580
I'm Ami Futami.

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:15.080
Tropical Juice

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:15.660
Here you are.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:16.700
Thank you.

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:20.870
Um, you're really good
at the piano, aren't you?

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:25.450
No, not at all. I used to play it
a little more when I was younger,

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:27.200
but lately I just don't have time...

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:31.500
I'm sorry for suddenly dropping in
while you're so busy.

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:33.750
I should be apologizing.

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:37.410
You've contacted me so many times,
but I've been unable to respond...

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:39.660
N-no, not at all!

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:42.250
She sure is polite, huh?

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:43.250
Yes.

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:49.700
So, what you wanted to talk about
was Mondenkind?

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:52.370
Yes. They want you to come back.

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:56.620
The director said he could
definitely use your help.

00:07:56.790 --> 00:07:58.620
Well, I thought as much.

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:01.500
If they wanted me for something,
that's all it could have been.

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:03.040
Huh? Um...

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:09.120
By the way, Miss Amami, Miss Hagiwara,
what do you do for Mondenkind?

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:14.200
Oh. I'm an operator, and Haruka
is the Imber's Idolmaster.

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:17.040
Imber? The iDOL that had been sealed up?

00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:19.080
Wh-what was that?!

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:20.750
Iori?

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:21.500
M-me?!
Iori?

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:21.910
I thought she was in the bathroom...

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:23.330
Of course.
I thought she was in the bathroom...

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:25.410
It's you. You're the only one.

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:27.000
Really?

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:27.450
Yes.
Really?

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:28.620
Yes.
The director?

00:08:28.620 --> 00:08:29.450
It truly is fate.
I wonder what they're doing...

00:08:29.450 --> 00:08:30.290
For me to find a girl like you here today.
I wonder what they're doing...

00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:31.330
For me to find a girl like you here today.

00:08:31.700 --> 00:08:32.160
Please, I'll make sure you won't regret it.

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:34.000
Don't tell me this is my...
Please, I'll make sure you won't regret it.

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:35.080
Don't tell me this is my...
You must appear in my work!

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:37.830
Cinderella story!

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:43.830
Everyone! Say "Yay!"

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:45.290
Yay!

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:49.620
Um, are you all right?

00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:50.910
Yes...

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:52.950
Would you do this for me?

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:54.580
With pleasure!

00:08:55.000 --> 00:09:00.450
Ah, how splendid!
You truly were born for this role!

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:03.290
When our other person suddenly got sick,
I didn't know what we'd do...

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:03.620
But ah, I'm so glad!

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:04.540
Haruka?
But ah, I'm so glad!

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:07.790
Yayoi?

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:10.160
What on Earth are you doing here?

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:13.250
Ah! It's Forehead Sunshine!

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:15.200
The Cosplay Performer!

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:18.120
I don't want some cockroach
talking to me about cosplay!

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:20.040
Why you...!

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:22.910
There's no way some starfish
will get the better of me!

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:23.290
Hold on, hold on.
There's no way some starfish
will get the better of me!

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:24.540
Hold on, hold on.
I'm a star! A STAR!
Anyway, you're still a cockroach!

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:26.910
I'm a star! A STAR!
Anyway, you're still a cockroach!

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:29.750
I could be a cricket and
not a cockroach, right?!

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:31.160
You're a cockroach!

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:34.950
Ami
Futami

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:34.950
You really are busy, aren't you?

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:39.950
A photo shoot, an interview,
then a meet and greet. After this...

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:43.620
A concert rehearsal and
three TV recordings.

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:45.500
Whoa, that's tough!

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:50.790
I'm sorry. I really wanted to speak
a little more leisurely, but...

00:09:50.830 --> 00:09:56.000
Not at all. It was wrong of us
to suddenly show up. Um, but...

00:09:56.250 --> 00:09:59.500
What should I tell
the director and the others?

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:01.580
Ah. That's right.

00:10:01.750 --> 00:10:03.200
Please wait a moment.

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:05.620
Okay.

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:10.750
Please give this to the supervisor.

00:10:13.790 --> 00:10:15.580
This is... a data card?

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:16.870
Haruka.

00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:21.290
You should quit being an Idolmaster.

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:26.040
The iDOLs can only bring people sadness.

00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:29.080
Ami?

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:33.750
So! You tried too hard,
and THIS is the result, huh?

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:38.160
Honestly! She sure is uppity
for a Cosplay Performer.

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:39.450
Well, no matter.

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:43.870
It was MY appearance that made an
indelible impression in the director's mind!

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:45.370
I wonder...

00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:48.250
Hey! Quit sleeping and
hurry up and feed me!

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:50.620
Jeez, I can't use my arms, so get your act-

00:10:53.830 --> 00:10:56.700
U-um, I can't eat something that big!

00:10:56.750 --> 00:10:57.330
Ow, that's hot! Stop it!

00:10:57.330 --> 00:10:58.870
Anyway, Ribbon sure is late...
Ow, that's hot! Stop it!

00:10:58.870 --> 00:11:00.450
Anyway, Ribbon sure is late...

00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:04.120
Yes. This is her answer.

00:11:04.370 --> 00:11:06.540
What is it?

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:09.000
Want to give it a listen?

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:10.910
It's a good song.

00:11:15.410 --> 00:11:16.580
All right.

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:22.290
This song!

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:42.290
It probably holds the song that Ami
made here long ago. With the iDOLs.

00:11:42.790 --> 00:11:46.540
The iDOLs can only bring people sadness.

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:10.870
Mami!

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:16.620
All right, we're starting the test!

00:12:17.160 --> 00:12:18.700
System checks are okay.

00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:20.620
All connections have been confirmed.

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:22.910
Okay. Hotoke, you good?

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:24.450
Yes, probably.

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:27.790
Nazuna, here we go. Begin!

00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:32.410
Gotcha. Maintenance initiation key, ignition!

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:38.540
Initiation confirmed.

00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:40.200
Hotoke, begin.

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:43.410
Understood. Beginning Harmonizer.

00:12:46.580 --> 00:12:49.040
All right. Keep it steady like that.

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:52.450
Stop it, hurry!

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:59.040
Chief! It's impossible!

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:01.830
We have no idea about
timbres or whatever.

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:04.500
Looks tough.

00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:06.540
Here.

00:13:06.750 --> 00:13:13.540
Thanks. We give up! I told the supervisor
we can't do it without Ami.

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:18.040
She said there's little chance
she'll come back to Mondenkind,

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:20.450
so make it work on our own somehow.

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:23.160
Jeez! You can't just say something like that!

00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:25.290
This is her answer.

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:30.450
Ribbon?

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:40.000
Makoto! Where's the supervisor?

00:13:40.950 --> 00:13:45.080
Ami Futami won't come back.
No matter what.

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:57.290
Koi da mon, ii ja nai no
I mean, it's love, where's the harm?

00:13:57.290 --> 00:13:59.700
Minogashite
Overlook it

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:02.750
Dou shiyo, dou shiyo nante
"What should I do, what should I do?"

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:04.950
Yumeutsutsu
Is like a dream

00:14:03.620 --> 00:14:07.330
We've had the same exchange
a few times before.

00:14:04.950 --> 00:14:09.580
Koi da mon, mucha na shoubu totsugeki yo
I mean, it's love, a reckless assault for the win

00:14:07.410 --> 00:14:11.580
I thought maybe she'd change her mind
if she met you, but...

00:14:09.580 --> 00:14:16.910
Ganbaru wa, ouen shite! "Suki yo, suki yo!"
I'll do my best, root for me! "I like you, I like you!"

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:16.580
Thank you. Don't worry
about it anymore, Haruka.

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:25.120
Hello? Yayoi?

00:14:26.040 --> 00:14:28.450
Ami Futami's schedule?

00:14:28.830 --> 00:14:31.450
Uh, I think I can find it if I try...

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:35.290
First Departure 4:08
To Asakusa
Next Departure 4:12

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:36.370
Oh, here. It looks like she's doing
nothing but voice lessons.

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:41.080
Next week, she has a concert at Yoyogi
Stadium. Must be nice to be so popular.

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:43.580
Looks like I'll have to go back to
department store management.

00:14:44.330 --> 00:14:46.000
Yes, okay!

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:50.160
Okay, let's do the hook next.
Huh? Who are you?

00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:53.870
Um, well, I'm certainly no one suspicious.

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:55.040
Excuse me.

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:58.910
Please let me take a little break.

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:02.700
I'm sorry for bothering you like this...

00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:05.580
Not at all. But I was surprised.

00:15:06.950 --> 00:15:09.870
I thought we'd said all there was to say.

00:15:09.870 --> 00:15:13.040
Oh, yes. But there was
something that bothered me...

00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:14.200
Bothered you?

00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:18.330
Ami, you said the iDOLs
only bring sadness.

00:15:18.330 --> 00:15:21.700
Why would you say something like that?

00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:26.870
I mean, Imber... The iDOLs have hearts.

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:30.080
There are sad times, but happy times, too.

00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:31.410
No, there aren't.

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:34.910
Being with the iDOLs is only painful.

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:36.040
"Only"?

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:38.330
I know that now.

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:43.750
You hate the iDOLs that much?

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:44.540
Yes.

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:45.540
But...!

00:15:45.620 --> 00:15:47.830
My younger sister is dead.

00:15:50.830 --> 00:15:54.870
She was killed. By an iDOL.

00:15:56.580 --> 00:15:59.290
That song from before was made by

00:15:59.290 --> 00:16:03.580
me, my sister Mami, and
Tempestas, the three of us.

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:08.580
We made sounds together.
And yet Tempestas...

00:16:09.120 --> 00:16:10.580
Ami...

00:16:10.620 --> 00:16:15.290
You get it now, don't you?
The iDOLs destroyed everything.

00:16:15.500 --> 00:16:21.830
My hopes, Mami's hopes...
All of it, everything!

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:24.870
Everything!

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:26.160
How is it?

00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:29.580
There's still a margin of error.
Get it solved by morning.

00:16:29.790 --> 00:16:30.790
Huh?!

00:16:30.790 --> 00:16:32.700
You want to make us work late AGAIN?!

00:16:32.700 --> 00:16:34.370
It's your job, isn't it?

00:16:34.370 --> 00:16:35.330
Hey, hang-

00:16:40.790 --> 00:16:42.080
Amami?

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:51.330
iDOLs kill people?
Does that really happen?

00:16:51.870 --> 00:16:52.830
What are you...?

00:16:52.830 --> 00:16:55.700
What happened to Mami?

00:16:55.700 --> 00:17:00.830
What did Tempestas do?
You know, don't you?

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:02.870
What did Futami say?

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:06.120
She said everything was destroyed.

00:17:08.870 --> 00:17:09.870
Is that so.

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:13.870
It went out of control.

00:17:14.370 --> 00:17:17.120
Prometheus 4. The Tempestas.

00:17:18.410 --> 00:17:23.290
Ami and Mami, twins, believed
the iDOLs had hearts.

00:17:23.450 --> 00:17:28.330
That the three of them together would
protect the world. That's what they said.

00:17:29.870 --> 00:17:30.540
And yet...

00:17:31.830 --> 00:17:33.540
Prometheus 4 can't be controlled!

00:17:33.830 --> 00:17:34.830
Output continues to rise from earlier levels!

00:17:34.830 --> 00:17:36.250
Gravity quake confirmed!
Output continues to rise from earlier levels!

00:17:36.250 --> 00:17:37.580
What about the stop signal?

00:17:37.580 --> 00:17:38.870
We've been sending it!

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:47.580
Mami! Tempestas!

00:17:48.450 --> 00:17:49.700
"I'm sor..."

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:51.620
What?!

00:17:51.660 --> 00:17:55.290
Tempestas says, "I'm sorry."

00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:04.450
Mami... Mami!

00:18:06.250 --> 00:18:08.200
The accident was caused by

00:18:08.200 --> 00:18:13.290
a misplaced belief that feelings
were being transmitted to the iDOL,

00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:15.120
that they were interacting.
It caused deep wounds.

00:18:15.370 --> 00:18:20.410
iDOLs don't kill people.
That was just an accident.

00:18:21.790 --> 00:18:23.410
I don't really understand.

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:25.700
Imber...

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:31.040
This is...

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:34.580
Maybe...

00:18:34.580 --> 00:18:37.080
Ami Futami
DEBUT ALBUM!!!!
"Don't Forget the Positive"
IN 5 DAYS

00:18:37.500 --> 00:18:41.200
This is Point S. The target has just
arrived at the stadium.

00:18:41.290 --> 00:18:42.330
Thank you.

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:44.080
Please keep up the surveillance.

00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:47.830
Ma'am. But is it okay? Doing this...

00:18:47.830 --> 00:18:49.330
I'll leave the letter of apology to you.

00:18:49.580 --> 00:18:50.540
Huh?!

00:18:51.750 --> 00:18:53.750
Good morning!

00:18:55.120 --> 00:18:58.370
No one's here?
I thought today was rehearsals...

00:18:58.790 --> 00:19:01.040
The target has passed through Point G.

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:03.790
Prometheus 1 is moving
from Channel 3 to 4.

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:06.370
I want no part of this!

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:21.660
How flashy...

00:19:27.500 --> 00:19:29.200
An iDOL?

00:19:32.500 --> 00:19:33.620
Haruka?

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:38.580
Ah, sorry. But I really wanted
you to see Imber.

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:44.580
I heard from Makoto. I know
the reason you hate the iDOLs.

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:49.790
But Tempestas said
something at the end, right?

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:54.330
I'm sure he was trying
to tell you something.

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:56.250
If so...!

00:19:56.250 --> 00:19:58.500
Then he should just come back,
shouldn't he?!

00:19:58.500 --> 00:20:02.040
If he has something to say,
he should come tell me!

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:03.790
You're right.

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:09.330
I thought the same thing, too.
But even if he doesn't come back...

00:20:09.330 --> 00:20:13.160
Can you just turn away?
Can you plug your ears?

00:20:13.660 --> 00:20:20.040
At this rate, is the same as if Tempestas'
or Mami's sentiments never existed.

00:20:20.370 --> 00:20:22.830
Let's look for Tempestas.

00:20:22.830 --> 00:20:28.540
We have to look for him, and ask him.
Why he took Mami like that.

00:20:28.540 --> 00:20:30.620
Why he said "Sorry."

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:38.330
I'm sure he'll answer.
I mean, iDOLs have hearts.

00:20:42.790 --> 00:20:45.910
Imber came and looked for me.

00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:53.540
This is your song, pulled from
Tempestas' data left at Mondenkind, right?

00:21:05.830 --> 00:21:07.500
Ami...

00:21:08.410 --> 00:21:09.910
Mami.

00:21:20.660 --> 00:21:22.160
Good morning!

00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:25.080
All right, look alive!

00:21:25.330 --> 00:21:27.120
It's time to show your upperclassman
something good!

00:21:27.120 --> 00:21:28.620
Ma'am!

00:21:29.290 --> 00:21:31.040
You're full of energy first thing
in the morning.

00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:32.910
Oh, good morning.

00:21:32.910 --> 00:21:34.040
The truth is-

00:21:34.040 --> 00:21:35.450
Good morning.

00:21:43.250 --> 00:21:44.500
Ami!

00:21:44.500 --> 00:21:45.660
It's a promise.

00:21:45.660 --> 00:21:46.790
Huh?

00:21:46.790 --> 00:21:50.790
Be sure to find Tempestas for me, please.

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:53.500
Ami...

00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:55.330
Okay!

00:21:56.410 --> 00:22:05.370
Like a saint that crosses the ages

00:22:05.370 --> 00:22:14.330
In what kind of loneliness did you cry?

00:22:14.330 --> 00:22:23.200
Stretching out to a star so far away

00:22:23.200 --> 00:22:31.750
Say, I'll depict my feelings, look up at the sky

00:22:33.370 --> 00:22:43.200
Dear boy, if I always look for you in my heart

00:22:43.200 --> 00:22:52.160
Ah, I'll release a light so strong it will envelop you

00:22:52.160 --> 00:23:01.120
That sparkling trail will be the guide for us both

00:23:01.120 --> 00:23:12.700
Now, no matter where we look, we feel the truth

00:23:26.080 --> 00:23:41.080
Preview
Dissonance [Static]

00:23:27.160 --> 00:23:31.540
Miss Naze, they say girls
in glasses are popular, huh?

00:23:31.540 --> 00:23:32.330
Yeah.

00:23:32.330 --> 00:23:34.790
And they're incapable
of making mistakes, huh?

00:23:34.790 --> 00:23:35.870
I've heard that.

00:23:35.870 --> 00:23:38.540
So why are we-?

00:23:38.540 --> 00:23:39.580
Don't say it!
